mand in one order makes shortfalls a bit less likely. It ramps up for the day-22 spike in product 0. Overall I rate it at least neutral, probably good.\n- **2 and 5:** both are about 0.1 off the ideal, plan 2 below it and plan 5 above it, on both products. Their losses look roughly equal, so these two are close to a coin flip.\n- **0:** a flat 36/32 every day. It misses the day-22 spike in product 0 (forecast 71) and the day-23 spike in product 1 (forecast 52).\n- **6:** about 1.4× on product 0, which builds up stock that eventually spoils.\n- **1:** only about 0.8× on product 1, so it runs short a lot.\n\nMy expected top half is 7, 4, 3, plus one of 2 or 5."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 5050, "cache_read_input_tokens": 886, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 5050}, "output_tokens": 5, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-29T08:01:42.454Z", "request_id": "req_011CgWBDxsjcNakn2M1wXPP5"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01BaoWFtmiVQ1ynkEjVsizq2", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWBDy97T8bFGR2bHfB1t", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01BaoWFtmiVQ1ynkEjVsizq2", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {"p": [0.3, 0.15, 0.48, 0.6, 0.75, 0.45, 0.25, 0.75]}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "s